{"id": "q0436", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.04, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1374, "eot_read_ms": 17, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "transcript": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Daenerys Targaryen wants to rule Westeros because she believes it is her birthright. As the last surviving heir of the Targaryen dynasty, she sees herself as the rightful queen, destined to reclaim the Iron Throne for her family. Her desire is fueled by a sense of destiny, a belief in restoring justice and order through her rule, and a vision of a new era where dragons and noble leadership bring peace. While some see her ambition as noble others view it as dangerous—a powerful ruler determined to shape the future of the Seven Kingdoms.", "answer_ms": 2310}
